    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="1044" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-20T11:00:00+08:00">January 20, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 20—6 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. Legation’s 5, January 6, noon.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d844-f1"/> Following from
                    American Consul at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 19, 4 p.m. Nelson<anchor n="6" xml:id="d844-f2"/> has been taken
                            by his captors across the Hupeh border into Anhwei. I have notified
                            military authorities and again urged that some definite and sustained
                            effort be made to effect release. I suggest that the case be brought
                            once more to attention of Nanking authorities.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d844-f1" n="5" xml:id="d844-f1-content">
